      "title": "Two schools, one direction",
      "body": "I was formed by the Ukrainian creative school: structure, narrative, large casts, the discipline of big projects and productions. Alongside the work, I took daily class in the Vaganova method. The rest I learned from my New York colleagues: four years of daily class in Complexions and Balanchine technique with the teachers of Dwight Rhoden and Desmond Richardson's company, and a role in The Great Gatsby, choreographed by Rhoden. My movement language sits at the meeting point of those two schools, and that is exactly the line I bring to the French stage: European depth with an American engine.\nSince May 2026 I have lived in France, and I do one thing only — ballet."
