      "icareNote": "ICARE\nIgor Markevitch wrote L'Envol d'Icare in 1932 for Serge Lifar. Lifar refused: he could not bring his own rhythm into accord with the score, and in 1935 staged his own Icare with no music at all — to rhythms he set himself, the percussion added only after the choreography was finished. Markevitch's score has never been staged. Markevitch and Lifar were both born in Kyiv. The composer's own version is for two pianos and three percussionists: seven movements, 27 minutes. Bartók heard it; it is believed to have shaped his Sonata for Two Pianos and Percussion.",
